{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The fifth time</b><br>As in its interpretation. There you will find מדינה and in the words of Ahab you will find them." "איומה. [That there is awe upon all who see her] from איום ונורא." "כנדגלות. With the camps that have דגלים." "<b>The second time</b><br>He answered when he saw she was beautiful, like כנדגלות the camps bearing the standards — and behold, your hair is like a flock of goats, and your teeth like ewes, and like a slice of pomegranate your temple. And the meaning [is]: behold, these are signs that she is my beloved, the first one, and you shall not intermingle among the others, for you are one and none is like you. For behold, King Solomon has sixty queens, but my dove is one, and even the queens will praise her and marvel and say: Who is this who looks forth like the dawn?" "<b>The third time</b><br>The Shekhinah said: after you have returned in repentance and sought me, now you shall return to your kingdom as at first. And this is concerning the time of the Hasmonean sons, for from those days Israel ruled."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "[שם] resolved as 'there' (i.e., in that verse); the referent is uncertain.", 1 "The bracketed portion is a parenthetical gloss on the word; איום ונורא left untranslated as it is the liturgical phrase being cited as the etymological source.", 2 "דגלים left in Hebrew as a technical term (standards/banners of the wilderness camps).", 3 "Bracketed Hebrew insertions ([ה], [היא], [כי אחת את ואין דומה]) appear to be textual glosses or corrections in the source; translated as integral to the sentence where the syntax requires.", 4 "[ה] before שכינה resolved as the definite article."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:48.387047163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}